275	// replaceBinary moves src over dest atomically. On Windows, a running
276	// executable can't be replaced (sharing violation) but it *can* be renamed:
277	// move the old binary aside to a .old-<rand> file and retry; leftovers are
278	// swept on the next install. os.Rename fails across filesystems (staging is
279	// in the system temp dir), so a copy fallback covers that case.
